WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.493
DeepMind asks

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:02.508
what comes after

00:00:02.319 --> 00:00:03.097
AGI

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:04.868
A DeepMind essay

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:05.587
argues that with

00:00:05.411 --> 00:00:06.707
AGI within reach

00:00:06.944 --> 00:00:07.816
AI could keep

00:00:07.628 --> 00:00:09.302
advancing toward artificial

00:00:09.114 --> 00:00:10.587
superintelligence or

00:00:10.434 --> 00:00:11.200
ASI

00:00:11.734 --> 00:00:13.019
Training compute needed

00:00:12.831 --> 00:00:13.561
for a fixed

00:00:13.373 --> 00:00:14.658
performance level has

00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:15.826
fallen roughly three

00:00:15.637 --> 00:00:16.734
to six times

00:00:16.545 --> 00:00:17.300
per year

00:00:17.439 --> 00:00:18.275
Combined

00:00:18.359 --> 00:00:19.820
effective compute grows

00:00:19.632 --> 00:00:20.622
at least ten

00:00:20.434 --> 00:00:21.448
times a year

00:00:21.974 --> 00:00:22.882
At that rate

00:00:23.094 --> 00:00:24.108
work costing a

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:25.075
billion dollars in

00:00:24.887 --> 00:00:26.160
compute today would

00:00:25.972 --> 00:00:26.997
cost just a

00:00:26.809 --> 00:00:27.999
thousand dollars in

00:00:27.811 --> 00:00:28.766
ten years

00:00:29.286 --> 00:00:30.300
Full story on

00:00:30.111 --> 00:00:31.007
the dashboard
